QuestGuidance.Register("en",84,{
[2657]="70008182\n1\tRepair broken sections of fences (total: 6)\tBroken fence-pieces can be found at Nathan Hodges' Farm in the northern Lone-lands, near Annúndir. You should repair the broken fences, in case the Hodges wish to return.\n2\tCompleted\tYou have done a kindness to the Hodges, for there will be less work for them when they return.\n",
[2658]="7003E410\n1\tFertilize Carnimírië's Seed at the Easeful Mead\030Gather clumps of sandy soil (total: 4)\tQuickbeam believes the seed needs to be covered with sandy soil in order to continue to grow. Sandy soil can be found along the river in Fangorn Forest.\n2\tReturn to Quickbeam\tQuickbeam needs to ponder how best to support the seed's growth. Return to Quickbeam at Derndingle to hear what he has to say.\n3\tSpeak to Quickbeam\tQuickbeam has figured out what soil is next needed for the seed. Quickbeam is ready to speak to you at Derndingle.\n4\tFertilize Carnimírië's Seed at the Easeful Mead\030Gather clumps of mossy soil (total: 6)\tQuickbeam believes the seed needs to be covered with mossy soil in order to continue to grow. Mossy soil can be found at Wellinghall in Fangorn.\n5\tReturn to Quickbeam\tQuickbeam needs to ponder how best to support the seed's growth. Return to Quickbeam at Derndingle to hear what he has to say.\n6\tSpeak to Quickbeam\tQuickbeam has figured out what soil is next needed for the seed. Quickbeam is ready to speak to you at Derndingle.\n7\tFertilize Carnimírië's Seed at the Easeful Mead\030Gather clumps of chunky soil (total: 4)\tQuickbeam believes the seed needs to be covered with chunky soil in order to continue to grow. Chunky soil can be found in the north-east of Fangorn.\n8\tReturn to Quickbeam\tQuickbeam needs to ponder how best to support the seed's growth. Return to Quickbeam at Derndingle to hear what he has to say.\n9\tSpeak to Quickbeam\tQuickbeam has figured out what soil is next needed for the seed. Quickbeam is ready to speak to you at Derndingle.\n10\tFertilize Carnimírië's Seed at the Easeful Mead\030Gather clumps of rocky soil (total: 4)\tQuickbeam believes the seed needs to be covered with rocky soil in order to continue to grow. Rocky soil can be found along the mountains north-east of Derndingle.\n11\tReturn to Quickbeam\tQuickbeam needs to ponder how best to support the seed's growth. Return to Quickbeam at Derndingle to hear what he has to say.\n12\tSpeak to Quickbeam\tQuickbeam has figured out what soil is next needed for the seed. Quickbeam is ready to speak to you at Derndingle.\n13\tFertilize Carnimírië's Seed at the Easeful Mead\030Gather clumps of cold soil (total: 4)\tQuickbeam believes the seed needs to be covered with cold soil in order to continue to grow. Cold soil can be found along the mountains in the south-west of Fangorn.\n14\tReturn to Quickbeam\tQuickbeam wishes to speak with you about the seed you have been growing. Quickbeam is at Derndingle.\n",
[2659]="7001AF8F\n1\tDefeat crawlers and rats in the northern Barrow-downs (total: 24)\tCrawlers and rats can be found throughout the northern Barrow-downs and these vermin are likely carriers of disease. You have been asked to kill these creatures so that the refugees hiding at the camp between the Barrow-downs and the Old Forest will have a clear path to follow when they leave. Sal Haywood believes that you can help her create a path for the Bree-folk to follow when the time comes for them to move. She asked you to rid the Barrow-downs of many of the vermin therein.\n2\tTalk to Sal Haywood between the Old Forest and Barrow-downs\tSal Haywood rests with the others at the makeshift camp between the Barrow-downs and the Old Forest. You fought and slew a good number of the disease-bearing creatures that make the Barrow-downs their home. You should return to Sal Haywood with the news.\n",
[2660]="70066A6A\n1\tReport to Lúmar in Ost Arndír\tIgerna has sent you on to Ost Arndír with her report of the goblin incursion. You should bring the report to Lúmar and let him know what you and Igerna have been doing.\n",
[2661]="7004DA62\n1\tCollect crude stones from the slopes of Erebor (total: 12)\tCrude stones can be found along the western slopes of Erebor. Ambassador Spakorth has asked you to gather crude stones from the slopes of Erebor that they might be carved into rune-stones by the Stout-axes.\n2\tStout-axe rune-carvers can be found in Erebor. You have gathered many stones from the slopes of Erebor and should now deliver them to the Stout-axe rune-carvers in Erebor.\t\n3\tCompleted\tYou have delivered many crude stones to the Stout-axe rune-carvers.\n",
[2662]="70008852\n1\tReturn to Chieftain Torbok at the Grimwood Lumber-camp\030Collect Grimwood-heartwood (total: 10)\tGrimwood-heartwood can be found on the Leafcull-trees, though you may possibly find it in the fallen logs as well. Chieftain Torbok directed you to recover and return Grimwood-heartwood to him.\n",
[2663]="70067F63\n1\tCollect wine casks (total: 6)\tAhuz has asked you to retrieve his lost wine casks. His boat ran ashore to the west of Mâr Naphra.\n2\tDeliver casks to Ahuz\tYou have successfully collected all of Ahuz's wine casks. You should return them. Ahuz can be found in Mâr Naphra.\n",
[2664]="700583F6\n1\tBurn the stone-claw corpses within Klórgren\tThe burrows of Klórgren can be found on the eastern edges of Elderslade. You should burn the stone-claw corpses within Klórgren.\n2\tBurn the stone-claw corpses within Klórgren (total: 10)\tThe burrows of Klórgren can be found on the eastern edges of Elderslade. You should burn the stone-claw corpses within Klórgren.\n3\tCompleted\tBurn many stone-claw corpses within Klórgren.\n",
[2665]="7006EC20\n1\tComplete Quest: Yes to Cats\030Complete Quest: No to Cats\tMaghôrdo is unsure of what to do about the cats. He has asked for your opinion - should they stay or should they go?\n2\tTalk to Maghôrdo\tMaghôrdo asked for your opinion on what should be done about Furtherholm's cats. You made a decision and acted accordingly. You should report to Maghôrdo at Furtherholm's harbour, near the waterfall.\n",
[2666]="7006EC1F\n1\tShoo the scruffy cat\030Shoo the slinky cat\030Shoo the skinny cat\030Shoo the smelly cat\030Shoo the sleepy cat\030Shoo the sassy cat\tMaghôrdo has asked you to visit each cat in Furtherholm's harbour area and shoo them away.\n2\tReturn to Maghôrdo\tYou have shoo'd away each cat in Furtherholm's harbour. You should report to Maghôrdo at Furtherholm's harbour, near the waterfall.\n",
[2667]="7006EC1B\n1\tFeed the scruffy cat\030Feed the slinky cat\030Feed the skinny cat\030Feed the smelly cat\030Feed the sleepy cat\030Feed the sassy cat\tMaghôrdo has asked you to visit each cat in Furtherholms harbour area and give them a bite to eat.\n2\tReturn to Maghôrdo\tYou have given each cat in Furtherholm's harbour area a bite to eat. You should report to Maghôrdo at Furtherholm's harbour, near the waterfall.\n",
[2668]="70066739\n1\tGive treats to the friendly cat\030Give treats to the irate cat\030Give treats to the disinterested cat\030Give treats to the self-satisfied cat\tOld Grathir has asked you to give treats to the cats around Lothgobel.\n2\tTalk to Old Grathir\tTell Old Grathir that you have given out the treats as he asked. Old Grathir can be found near the southern entrance of Lothgobel.\n",
[2669]="7000E76A\n1\tCollect kalpa-kita tusks (total: 20)\tKalpa-kita can be found in and around their den at Leijona-kotin, as well as roaming the rest of Itä-ma. Kimmo has asked you to bring him some tusks from the kalpa-kita which roam Forochel.\n2\tReturn to Kimmo with the kalpa-kita tusks\tKimmo is at Pynti-peldot. You should return to him with the kalpa-kita tusks.\n",
[2670]="700413C6\n1\tCollect fish from the nets along the river-bank (total: 5)\tFish can be found in the nets that run along the river-bank of the river Ringló. You should collect fish from the nets.\n2\tInvestigate what washed up on the river-bank\tThe village of Ethring is located in Ringló Vale. Investigate what washed up on the river-bank in Ethring.\n3\tExamine the body\tThe body is in the village of Ethring. You should examine the body.\n4\tSpeak with Laerind\tLaerind is located in the village of Ethring. You should tell Laerind of what you have seen.\n",
[2671]="700529E5\n1\tCatch Great River trout (total: 3)\tFishing poles can be found at the river docks in Arhaim. You should check the fishing poles for bites.\n2\tTalk to Tassila\tTassila can be found at the river docks in Arhaim. You should bring the trout to Tassila.\n",
[2672]="70057192\n1\tCatch lost chickens (total: 4)\tLost chickens can be found in the Beorninglands near the Beorninghús. You should catch the lost chickens for Grimbeorn.\n2\tReturn to the Beorninghús\tYou should bring the lost chickens back to the Beorninghús.\n",
[2673]="700686AA\n1\tTalk to Nekhama across the way from Gûshida\tEzôti is nowhere to be found, but Gûshida and a familiar face from the Shield Isles are here. Speak to Gûshida and Nekhama in the Upper Ward.\n",
[2674]="7005AB18\n1\tRescue harassed ice-giants (total: 6)\tSeveral ice-giants have been caught between the battle between the Orcs and hobgoblins. You should rescue harassed ice-giants in Thyrstáth.\n2\tCall Hórin and talk to him\tUse the summoning horn to call Hórin to your side. You should talk to Hórin.\n",
[2675]="70054674\n1\tRescue ambushed Rangers (total: 5)\tAmbushed Rangers can be found in the Circle of Madness. You should rescue ambushed Rangers.\n2\tTalk to Rhadrog\tRhadrog is stationed inside Barad Elenath, the Star-gazers' Spire. You should talk to Rhadrog.\n",
[2676]="700164D7\n1\tTalk to Geirfast in the Twenty-First Hall\030Collect Brooch of Lórien\tGeirfast is in the Twenty-first Hall. The brooch of Lórien you found is marked with the name Geirfast.\n",
[2677]="700272D6\n1\tPlace the ale in the guard's post when the shift changes\tDaervunn the Ranger is detained at the Ford of Isen. When the current guard leaves, put the ale someplace where Arbald is likely to stumble upon it.\n2\tRelease Daervunn when Arbald falls asleep. Be careful not to let him see you\tDaervunn the Ranger is detained at the Ford of Isen. You should wait until Arbald drinks himself into a stupour, then cut the imprisoned Ranger loose, but be careful not to let the guard spot you. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n",
[2678]="7000700D\n1\tSpeak with Istuienn\tIstuienn is in Esteldín. You should speak with Istuienn.\n2\tDeliver the letter to Asikko\tAsikko, chieftain of the Suuri-lehmä, can be found at the Earth-kin camp located along the hills north of the eastern entrance to Esteldín. Istuienn asked you for a favour; she gave you a letter and sent you to find Asikko, the chieftain of the Earth-kin still loyal to the defence of Ram Dúath.\n",
[2679]="70063010\n1\tSteal pins (total: 6)\tIago Rhudd has asked you to remove metal pins from the siege engines of Sharmokal. Sharmokal is located in southern Swanfleet.\n2\tBring the pins to Iago\tYou should bring the metal pins to Iago. Iago Rhudd is in Lintrev.\n",
[2680]="70060015\n1\tClear the mould from Eiricháv (total: 10)\tEiricháv can be found in north west Câr Bronach. You should clear the mould from Eiricháv.\n2\tTalk to Fuisach\tEiricháv can be found in north west Câr Bronach. You should talk to Fuisach.\n",
[2681]="700369FD\n1\tDefeat all enemies and protect Gimli\030Defeat the Troll Brute\tHelp the Rohirrim soldiers to defend the barricades and defeat the enemies coming from the cavern before Gimli is forced to cave in the entrance.\n",
[2682]="700380E6\n1\tDefeat all enemies and protect Gimli\tHelp the Rohirrim soldiers to defend the barricades and defeat the enemies coming from the cavern before Gimli is forced to cave in the entrance.\n",
[2683]="7000729D\n1\tDefeat Milkeyes within Rath Teraig (total: 9)\tMilkeyes can be found beyond the barricades south of the dwarf-camp. Tralli Hammerfist has asked you to enter Rath Teraig and kill off a number of Milkeyes, to prevent them from gnawing at the barricades.\n2\tTalk to Tralli Hammerfist\tTralli Hammerfist is at his camp beyond the barricade at the northern entrance to Rath Teraig. You should return to Tralli Hammerfist and let him know that you have done as he asked.\n",
[2684]="7001928B\n1\tDefeat cave-claws (total: 4)\tCave-claws are found near the buildings and caves to the east of Thorin's Gate and inside the Rockbelly Pit caves near Winterheight, south-east of the Frerin's Court. Bolli asked you to defeat cave-claws found throughout Thorin's Gate.\n2\tTalk to Bolli in Frerin's Court\tBolli can be found in Frerin's Court. You should return to Bolli with news of your success.\n",
[2685]="70028CAB\n1\tCollapse cave-openings (total: 3)\tThe cave-openings can be found along the hills east of Innoth's encampment. Innoth has asked you to collapse the cave-openings from whence the Orcs have been issuing.\n2\tTalk to Innoth near the Isen\tInnoth is at his camp near the Isen, west of the caves. You should return to Innoth with news of your success.\n",
[2686]="7004961B\n1\tDefeat fire-drakelings and destroy drakeling nests in Nargroth\tNargroth is located in Talath Úrui. You should defeat fire-drakelings and destroy drakeling nests in Nargroth.\n2\tDefeat fire-drakelings in Nargroth (total: 10)\030Destroy drakeling nests in Nargroth (total: 5)\tNargroth is located in Talath Úrui. You should defeat fire-drakelings and destroy drakeling nests in Nargroth.\n3\tCompleted\tDefeated fire-drakelings and destroyed drakeling nests in Nargroth.\n",
[2687]="70050B43\n1\tClear the entrance to the Spider Tunnels\tClear the entrance to the Spider Tunnels.\n2\tSecure the path leading to Etterfang\tSecure the path leading to Etterfang.\n3\tFind and defeat Etterfang Foulmaw\tFind and defeat Etterfang Foulmaw.\n",
[2688]="7004E748\n1\tClear the entrance to the Spider Tunnels\tClear the entrance to the Spider Tunnels.\n2\tSecure the path leading to Etterfang\tSecure the path leading to Etterfang.\n3\tFind and defeat Etterfang Foulmaw\tFind and defeat Etterfang Foulmaw.\n",
